<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n108840" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπονέμομαι</span></b> , 
			Med.
		, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>eat away
			beneath</i> or <i>secretly,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔλαθεν πῦρ ὑπονειμάμενον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					7.444
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Theaet.
			</span></i>); but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπονεμησαμένη,</span>
			though found in codd. in <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Oss.</u>
				18
			</span></i>, is 
				f. l. for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπονης αμένη</span>
			, 
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπονέω.</span>
			
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>undermine</i> (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπόνομος</span>):
			metaph., <i>deceive,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γυναῖκας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Epich.
					9
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
